## Tuple binding

Tuple binding (Expressif.Syntax 0.42.0 and the matching runtime): ~subtract and subtract~
use the existing operator style for ~, and the callable retains its function/predicate
style. Tildes inside double-quoted or backtick strings retain the string style.

To verify generated artifacts, restore local .NET tools, run `npm ci --prefix tests`,
install Rouge 4.6.1, then run `./Test-Highlighters.ps1` from this directory. This
executes real TextMate and Rouge tokenization and validates Notepad++ UDL boundaries.
